"""
SAP Spare Part Creator (MM01) - HTB3 / Plant 0230            version 2
=======================================================================

Built from:
  * Manual_SP_creation_in_SAP_V4.docx   (what has to be filled)
  * the SAP GUI script recording (VBS)  (the exact screen-field IDs of your system)

What it does per Excel row
  0. Opens SAP Logon, connects to the system and logs on - only if SAP is not
     already open (with SSO nothing has to be typed).
  1. MM01 main record: Basic data 1 (+ DE/KO/ZH descriptions), Basic data 2,
     Classification, Purchasing, Foreign trade import, Purchase order text
     (EN + DE), MRP 1-4, Forecasting, Plant data/stor. 1-2, Warehouse mgmt 1-2,
     Accounting 1-2, Costing 1-2  ->  save  ->  new material number
  2. MM01 valuation type NEW (Accounting 1)
  3. MM01 valuation type UNV (Accounting 1)
  4. Writes the material number + status back into the Excel file.

Every field is first addressed with the ID from your recording
(e.g. wnd[0]/usr/tabsTABSPR1/tabpSP09/.../ctxtMARC-EKGRP). If SAP shows a
screen slightly differently, the script falls back to finding the field by its
technical name (MARC-EKGRP) or its label ("Purchasing Group").

Requirements (Windows PC with SAP GUI):
    pip install pywin32 openpyxl
    SAP GUI scripting enabled (you already recorded a script, so it is).

Usage:
    python sap_spare_part_creator.py SP_input_template.xlsx --validate
    python sap_spare_part_creator.py SP_input_template.xlsx --dry-run --rows 3
    python sap_spare_part_creator.py SP_input_template.xlsx --confirm
    python sap_spare_part_creator.py SP_input_template.xlsx
    python sap_spare_part_creator.py --inspect        (dump current SAP screen)
"""

